well, with mojo assuming you are an expert, you are doing probably 30 damage
on average. 
excalibur does d8 or d12 +10 damage more, if you get to skilled in two
weapon combat [max for a valk], you will have  no damage penalty or bonus
for two weaponing,  
so you will probably end up with 42 vs small and 44 vs large on average.
Thats about 1.4 times as much damage. The other factor is that you now have
two weapons to enchant- if you get them both to +7, you have +14 damage from
their enchantments alone.  

As far as AC, the first thing to remember with regards to negative AC is that
it doesnt work quite like positive AC. If your AC is positive, it is
subtracted from the monsters roll.  If your AC is negative, a random number
between -1 and your AC is subtracted from the mosnters roll.  Since I seem
to recall that your AC was in the -25 range, here are the chance of getting
hit by a level 15, 20, and 25 monster with -20 and with negative 25 AC:

 Mon LVL         -20 AC           -25 AC
 ----------------------------------------
  15              72%              60%
  20              86%              78%
  25              89%              90%

[this assumes they can see you, arent trapped, etc]
The other effect of AC is that ACs better than -10 can reduce the damage
that you take,  the difference between -25 and -20 on this front is the
difference between a random number between 1 and 4 and a random number
between 1 and 3.

Id go with the two weapons- the best defense is a good offence- do unto them
before they do unto you.
